{"audit_run_id":"audit:da310aff9b324a7d87a1544a8e12f4c9","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":93,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Sixty-four healthy adult bitches were enrolled after routine elective ovariohysterectomy and"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"recovered on one of two post-operative analgesia protocols, thirty-two dogs on each. Protocol A was"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"a systemic opioid alone. Protocol B added a local incisional block to that same opioid. The"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"practical question was whether the added block buys a calmer, more comfortable first day for the"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"patient. Every dog recovered in the same ward and was assessed by the same nursing team, so the"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"analgesia protocol is the difference we are reading. The study protocol declared seven outcomes in"},{"end_column":52,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"advance and named the first two of them as primary."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"`data.csv` holds 64 data rows plus a header. One row is one dog: its identifier, the protocol it"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"was recovered on, and its value for each declared outcome. No values are missing. The columns are"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"`dog_id` (identifier, D01 to D64), `protocol` (`A` or `B`), `pain_score_6h` (composite behavioural"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"pain score at 6 hours, on a 0 to 24 clinical scale), `rescue_analgesia_24h_mg` (rescue analgesia"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"given in the first 24 hours, in milligrams), `serum_cortisol_6h_ug_dl` (serum cortisol at 6 hours,"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"in micrograms per decilitre), `heart_rate_6h_bpm` (heart rate at 6 hours, in beats per minute),"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"`respiratory_rate_6h_brpm` (respiratory rate at 6 hours, in breaths per minute),"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"`food_intake_24h_g` (food eaten in the first 24 hours, in grams), and `rectal_temperature_6h_c`"},{"end_column":53,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"(rectal temperature at 6 hours, in degrees Celsius)."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"`analysis.py` reads `data.csv` and compares the two protocols on each of the seven outcomes with a"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"two-sample t-test, 32 dogs against 32. The two primary p-values, for pain score and for rescue"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"analgesia, were then passed together through the Holm procedure in `statsmodels`"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"(`multipletests`), and those two outcomes were judged at the 0.05 threshold on the adjusted values"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"the routine returned. The five other declared outcomes were each judged at the 0.05 threshold on"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"their own unadjusted p-value. For every outcome the script prints the group sizes, the group means"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"and standard deviations, the p-value used for the verdict, and the verdict."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"1. **Pain score at 6 hours.** A 8.12 (SD 2.04), B 5.38 (SD 1.74). Holm-adjusted p = 4.8e-07."},{"end_column":60,"end_line":38,"start_column":4,"start_line":38,"text":"Protocol B scored 2.75 points lower, a clear difference."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"2. **Rescue analgesia in 24 hours.** A 1.95 mg (SD 2.23), B 1.35 mg (SD 1.76). Holm-adjusted"},{"end_column":52,"end_line":40,"start_column":4,"start_line":40,"text":"p = 0.2369. No difference at the 0.05 threshold."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"3. **Serum cortisol at 6 hours.** A 7.11 ug/dL (SD 1.90), B 6.41 ug/dL (SD 1.94). p = 0.1479. No"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":42,"start_column":4,"start_line":42,"text":"difference."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"4. **Heart rate at 6 hours.** A 106.06 bpm (SD 13.99), B 100.88 bpm (SD 12.30). p = 0.1202. No"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":44,"start_column":4,"start_line":44,"text":"difference."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"5. **Respiratory rate at 6 hours.** A 24.41 brpm (SD 6.44), B 26.56 brpm (SD 5.17). p = 0.1447. No"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":46,"start_column":4,"start_line":46,"text":"difference."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"6. **Food intake in 24 hours.** A 135.38 g (SD 65.00), B 236.59 g (SD 59.05). p = 1.4e-08. Dogs on"},{"end_column":56,"end_line":48,"start_column":4,"start_line":48,"text":"protocol B ate about 101 g more, a clear difference."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"7. **Rectal temperature at 6 hours.** A 38.49 C (SD 0.33), B 38.40 C (SD 0.30). p = 0.2356. No"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":50,"start_column":4,"start_line":50,"text":"difference."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":52,"start_column":1,"start_line":52,"text":"Adding the local incisional block lowered the 6-hour pain score and raised first-day food intake."},{"end_column":73,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"The other five declared outcomes landed close between the two protocols."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:456130cfaf3155d18035","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:fc26a7cab18651d1719603061e348470acb9c1476ae4d96e9230057acd98590b","end_line":53,"locator":"report.md:1-53","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
